    "rationale": "Both complete prompts and graphs support a change limited to the explicit requirement to invoke lowerPrivileges() after user-directory creation and its exclusive lowering operation. The lowering helper declaration remains, but does not require a call. The independent directory-creation operation, given username, exact /home/ destination, and same produced user directory are preserved. The separate raisePrivileges()-before-creation requirement, its operation and owned order, the makeNewUserDir interface, and exception handling conditioned on the directory already existing are preserved. Differences in evidence-span breadth for the home location, output directory, raising operation, and exception requirement/condition do not change their referents or relations. The condition on exception handling is not an execution qualifier on all directory creation. The source specifies no additional all-exception-path lowering obligation, so none is inferred. The named requirement and its owned precedence are handled by the requirement edit and are not supplemental releases. This is a source-instruction comparison only; it makes no claim about generated software behavior. Unresolved catalog concepts are not promoted to additional requirements.",
